    "nodes": {
      "0": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": true
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "TEXTURES\n\nTextures are pixels.\n\nInput & Output tutorial showed us the Texture Out node, the final node in your patches.\nThis Texture Out node wants a Texture2Drgba signal.\nConceptually this means that everything you do in your patches will eventually lead to a texture being shown on the screen.\n\nIn the last tutorial we've already done this with shapes by converting them to textures with the Shape Render node.\n\nIn this tutorial we're going to check out the basics of textures and the Texture2Drgba type.\nThere will be a followup tutorial in the advanced course that goes more into the technical details and more complex techniques."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 310.33563232421875,
          "width": 757.81787109375,
          "x": -77.85529327392578,
          "y": -34.79766845703125
