            "type": "bool",
            "value": false
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "EXAMPLE\n\nThis example is here to show you what kind of projects you will be able to make with textures once you've completed the basic course.\n\nWe are using a Texture In and Texture out to create a video effect patch.\n\nWe are using the Static video source with the Pixelate effect to get a texture made of large black and white chunks.\nThis texture is used as a mask for the Texture In node.\nWe also Invert the Texture In node and place that behind the masked texture using a Video Mixer.\n\nThis is all happening on the beat, provided by the Transport Beat node (which you'll learn more about soon!)\nMake sure to hit the play button in the transport bar (above the canvas) to get the BPM-sync going."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 716.1512451171875,
          "width": 1573.02001953125,
          "x": -77.94192504882812,
          "y": 1233.0849609375
