          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "COMBINING TEXTURES\n\nThe most common way to combine textures is through a Video Mixer.\nThis node will mix any amount of textures together with a given blend mode and an opacity for each input.\nThe size of the Video mixer can be changed in the Patch Panel.\n\nBut there are also alternatives, like Crossfader and Transition nodes that allow you to mix two textures.\n\nAssignment: create 3 video sources and add a single effect to each of them. Next, create a video mixer and blend them all together."
          }
        },
